# ── Odin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `odin build` names the executable after its package folder, so
# 2025/day01/ builds to 2025/day01/day01. Binary and folder share a
# name, so match the binary first and re-include the folder after:
# Git never descends into an excluded folder, and would otherwise
# hide every .odin source inside it.
day[0-9][0-9]
day[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]
day[0-9]
day[0-9]-[0-9][0-9]
day[_-][0-9][0-9]
day[_-][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]
day[_-][0-9]
day[_-][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]
!day[0-9]*/
!day[_-][0-9]*/
!*.odin
*.exe
# `odin build -file` writes <source stem> or <source stem>.bin
main
!main/
*.bin

# ── Puzzle input ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never committed: your personal input file.
*.input.txt
input.txt

# ── Neovim ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.sw[a-p]
*~
.netrwhist
tags
TAGS

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Merge leftovers ───────────────────────────────────────────────
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
build/
